;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; Gauntlet: hazards on the levels' own routes change. The tunables are in gauntlet-h.gc; pieces that live in a level's own file
;; call in through the functions it declares.
;;
;; Geyser Rock: a bomb drops on a spot from the drop-spot table when Jak comes within *gauntlet-bridge-trigger-radius*, and
;; re-arms once he is farther than *gauntlet-bridge-rearm-range*. One bomb at a time. The vent's trigger is a gate on the
;; bridge, and the bomb comes after Gol's warning, never before it.
;;
;; Every level: scout fly boxes ask for an eco colour to open (see "the scout fly boxes", hook in engine/common-obs/crates.gc).
;; Every level: nav-mesh enemies are born with clones ("the horde", hook in engine/entity/entity.gc). See also "the TNT barrels".
;;
;; The bomb is darkecobomb from the final boss (levels/finalboss/robotboss-weapon.gc), made available outside the Citadel:
;;   - its art group is in GAME.CGO (common_art_groups, game.gd) and its skelgroup asks for texture level 2;
;;   - the blast and warning particles are copied below from robotboss-part.gc under new ids (that file only loads with FIN.DGO);
;;   - the sounds are COMMON.SBK ones; the finale's own blast sound, explod-bomb, is in FINALBOS.SBK and would be silent here.
;;
;; It is blue: it pulls Jak in, glows blue and trails his blue aura. Its blast is drawn as a red wall at the blast radius and
;; a ring that grows to meet it as the bomb goes off (see gauntlet-ring). The ground is probed once, when the bomb appears.
;;
;; gauntlet-bomb is a bare process-drawable with a manipy for a body (as the Yellow Sage in levels/training/training-obs.gc),
;; so it has no collision. While counting down it pulls Jak with a collision-checked step each frame (fill-cache-for-shape!
;; then integrate-and-collide!, status restored), never a write to his velocity, which his control recomputes every frame.
;; On explosion it kills Jak inside the blast, unless a recent hit still has him invulnerable.

;; Tunables are globals with defaults in gauntlet-h.gc. Pull design: Jak runs 10 m/s and jumps 10 to 16 m/s, gravity is 60 m/s^2.
;; A runner starting under the bomb covers 40 m in the countdown against a 35 m blast, so the pull on foot must cost under 5 m.
(defconstant GAUNTLET_BOMB_FIRST_TICK 0.9) ;; the finale's warning curve: first beep when the clock reaches this cosine
(defconstant GAUNTLET_BOMB_TICK_STEP 0.06) ;; each beep lowers the bar by this, so beeps speed up
(defconstant GAUNTLET_GROUND_PROBE_UP (meters 2)) ;; the ground under Jak is searched from this far above his feet
(defconstant GAUNTLET_GROUND_PROBE_LENGTH (meters 20)) ;; ... and this far down
(defconstant GAUNTLET_BOMB_RING_PROBE_RAISE (meters 4)) ;; ground-probe height above where the bomb lands, so a rise in the ground does not bury the search
(defconstant GAUNTLET_PART_GROUP_BLAST 1000) ;; ids this file adds to the particle tables, above any the game uses
(defconstant GAUNTLET_PART_GROUP_TICK 1001)

;; ------------------------------------------------------------ the particles --

